      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:18xn29v'
    '|a||For space, both arrows pointed the same way: less. Must they always?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||The substitution arrow must. Make a good dearer and hold happiness fixed, and you always swap some of it away.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:s4ke01'
    '|a||And the income arrow? With more money, she''d rent more space.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1s3vobk'
    '|b||That makes space a normal good. But some things you buy precisely because money is tight.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1oydk0p'
    '|a||Say, in Harbourtown, the corner shop''s cheapest loaf. A family on a tight budget lives on it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:7wb3xo'
    '|b||Give that family more money and they switch to proper bakery bread. A good you buy less of as you get richer is called inferior. No snobbery: it only names the direction.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:slwjfp'
    '|a||So the shop raises the price of its cheapest loaf.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:gcug2x'
    '|a||Through the income effect alone, does the family buy more or less of the cheap loaf?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:l77vg4'
    '|a||More.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1280
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||More. Poorer, the family can afford even less bakery bread, so they lean harder on the cheap loaf.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||So here the two arrows pull in opposite directions.':
      mp3: 
