      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mxg6z'
    '|a||One answer, John Hicks''s: on the same indifference curve, equally happy. That''s the line we drew.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:exfmzt'
    '|b||Eugen Slutsky, back in 1915, said: enough money to still afford the old bundle A. Fewer assumptions about happiness.':
